From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:14:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] settings: Plugins can switch on a plugin that runs code as
 root

Since plugin API 1.6 a plugin may ship root scripts (root/install.sh,
update.sh, uninstall.sh; Kiln's docs/plugin-root-hooks.md). Klipper's
ad5x_plugins refuses ENABLE_PLUGIN for such a plugin unless ROOT=1 is
given, so Settings > Plugins (patch 0005) could not switch it on: the
switch sent ENABLE_PLUGIN NAME=<name>, Klipper answered with an error
and the switch went back. An install from the catalog with ENABLE=1
leaves such a plugin installed but off; the status line already shows
Klipper's message for that, and the plugin's row appears with its
switch off.

The status object's available[<name>].root is read into
Ad5xInstalledPlugin::root. Switching on a plugin with root set asks
first, in the panel's Warning confirmation: "This plugin runs some of
its code as root, the system's administrator account, for example to
set up USB devices. Turn it on only if you trust where it comes from.
Klipper restarts." Turn On sends ENABLE_PLUGIN NAME=<name> ROOT=1.
That starts a job (root/install.sh, shown on the status line as for an
install), and Klipper restarts only after root answers, so the command
is sent as one that does not restart right away (no "Firmware
restarting..." toast while install.sh runs). A job that fails
(install.sh refused, timed out) now also rebuilds the rows, so a switch
turned on for it goes back to off.

Plugins without root scripts, turning off, install, update and remove
ask and send what they did. The question and its command come from one
helper, ad5x_toggle_confirm(), so the tests can check them.

The new sentence is in every language of the screen. "Turn on {}?" was
only in English and Russian; it is added in the other nine, so the
question is in one language.

Tests: the installed rows carry root; switching a plugin without root
scripts on and off asks and sends as before; a root plugin's question
names root and the administrator account and sends ROOT=1 without an
immediate restart, and turning it off is unchanged; in every language
the root question and its title are translated (Russian checked word
for word).
